## Querying Attribute attributions

With a DoiT Attribute subscription, `data_source = "attribution"` queries the cost of one Attribute attribution. The query needs at least one `attribution_tier_1`, `attribution_tier_2` or `attribution_tier_3` dimension in `group`, `dimensions` or `filters`, and every tier dimension must use the same `id`: the attribution set ID with `-` replaced by `_`.

```terraform
data "doit_report_query" "team_costs" {
  config = {
    data_source   = "attribution"
    time_interval = "day"
    time_range = {
      mode            = "last"
      amount          = 30
      unit            = "day"
      include_current = true
    }
    group = [
      {
        id   = replace(var.attribution_set_id, "-", "_")
        type = "attribution_tier_1"
      }
    ]
  }
}
```

~> **Note:** Attribute attributions are unrelated to the deprecated `attribution` and `attribution_group` dimension types, which are the old names of allocation rules and allocations. See the [Attribute attributions guide](../guides/attribute_attributions).

